{"kind":"artifact","text":"The documentation citations at docs on exact head b422d4cde45d44313bfe38c095e54595f9d593ec. Eleven pages named 66b6cb0b at internal/statusview, which is retired; they now name 8aa25919, the live successor at that path published by merge 2c1443a6. Main is red without this: a retired citation is a withdrawn pointer rather than a moved world, and the gate refuses it.\n\nThis replaces b28187e8, which named the same head and the same content and could not be merged. I rested it on 8aa25919, and 8aa25919 rests on 66b6cb0b — the very record whose retirement this repairs — so the repair artifact inherited staleness from the thing it was repairing and gs merge refused the approval that named it.\n\nThis one rests on 24d800c0 at cmd/gs, which is live and not stale, and which carries the citation guard added by merge c7053206. That is the behaviour this whole episode is about: the guard refuses a retirement the documentation still cites, and it did not fire here because it is only wired into the CLI path and not the MCP one, recorded as 7f4416ae.\n\nThe pages themselves still cite 8aa25919 and that is correct. A stale citation is honest — it says a basis moved. Only a retired citation fails the gate.","body":{"commit":"b422d4cde45d44313bfe38c095e54595f9d593ec","path":"docs"}}